<div class="page">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Objectives</h2>
    <div class="content-body">
        <p>The purpose of this document is to enable new students to do the following:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Create a University "NetID"</li>
            <li>Access their university e-mail ("Student WebMail") account</li>
            <li>Log on to "WebCampus", the university's LMS ("Learning Management System")</li>
            <li>Access "WebAdvisor" to view grades, transcripts, financial aid documents, and tuition statements</li>
            <li>Locate their assigned online course sections in WebCampus</li>
            <li>Characterize the general organization and main content areas of a typical online course</li>
            <li>Identify additional sources of information, training, and support to aid in getting started with their online learning experience.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2 class="subsection-title">Obtaining access to information systems required for online learning</h2>
    <div class="content-body">
        <p>You will need to access several university systems in order to administer your online course.</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>FDU Net ID</strong><br>
                Universal login credential required to access most FDU systems.</li>
            <li><strong>Student WebMail (Office 365)</strong><br>
                As a matter of policy, your FDU E-mail account will be used for all correspondences related to your online course.</li>
            <li><strong>WebCampus (Blackboard)</strong><br>
                WebCampus is the university's implementation of the Blackboard "LMS", or "Learning Management System". It is a secure, password-protected platform for you to interact with instructor and fellow classmates, review course materials and feedback, and perform all other functions needed to learn online class.</li>
            <li><strong>WebAdvisor</strong><br>
                WebAdvisor provides pertinent information to students, staff and faculty. Its main purpose for students is to review class schedules, tuition information, and final grades.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Step 1: Create an FDU "Net ID"</h2>
    <div class="content-body">
        <p>All students need a NetID username and password before they can access other university systems.</p>
        <p>If you already have a functioning FDU NetID or E-mail address, you do not need to do this.</p>

        <p class="step-header">Steps to generate Net ID</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Point your Web browser to <a href="{{ netid_url }}">{{ netid_url }}</a>.
                <div class="image-placeholder">
                    <!-- Image Placeholder for NetID Login Screen -->
                    <p>Image of NetID Login Screen</p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li>Click "Request a NetID"</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="subsection-title">3. Enter the requested information.</h3>
        <div class="image-placeholder">
            <!-- Image Placeholder for Account Setup Form -->
            <p>Image of Account Setup Form</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note">
            <p><strong>Tips:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>On-line / Off-Campus students should select "Metropolitan Campus"</li>
                <li>Be sure to select "student" in the "Status" field.</li>
                <li>You will need your FDU student ID number to create a new "NetID"; contact <a href="{{ admissions_contact }}">{{ admissions_contact }}</a> if you do not know where to find this information.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <p>As soon as your details are verified, you will receive your FDU Email address and FDU NetID.</p>
        <p>Once your account is created, e-mail can be addressed to either your PRIMARY E-MAIL ADDRESS (e.g. {{ primary_email_example }}) or your LOGIN NAME (e.g. {{ login_name_example }}). For help and support with NetID, please contact the university help desk at {{ help_phone }} or visit <a href="{{ netid_help_url }}">{{ netid_help_url }}</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Step 2: Access your FDU Student Webmail account (Office 365)</h2>
    <div class="content-body">
        <p>Important note for existing FDU students</p>
        <p>On {{ migration_date }}, FDU migrated your student email account from Gmail to Office 365. The Gmail app on your mobile device, where you would normally receive your university information, has not received email since that day.</p>
        <p>To receive email on your mobile device moving forward, you will need to download the Outlook app and follow the instructions in the link below.</p>
        <p><em>"Accessing an FDU Email Account on a Mobile Device Using the Outlook App"</em></p>
        <p>As always, email is available at <a href="{{ webmail_url }}">{{ webmail_url }}</a> from your phone browser or computer.</p>

        <p>To access your FDU Student Webmail account, point your Web browser to <a href="{{ webmail_login_url }}">{{ webmail_login_url }}</a>. When prompted, enter your FDU NetID username and password to log on to Webmail.</p>

        <div class="image-placeholder">
            <!-- Image Placeholder for Webmail Login -->
            <p>Image of Webmail Login Screen</p>
        </div>

        <p style="margin-top: 20px;">Note: If you have not yet created a "NetID", click "Create New Account"</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="subsection-title">For Help and Support with Student Webmail (Gmail)</h2>
    <div class="content-body">
        <p>Students who experience difficulty accessing their Student WebMail accounts should contact the help desk at {{ webmail_support_phone }} or <a href="mailto:{{ webmail_support_email }}">{{ webmail_support_email }}</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="subsection-title">Related Resources</h2>
    <div class="content-body">
        <p>FDU Information Technologies Website: <a href="{{ fdu_tech_link }}">{{ fdu_tech_link }}</a></p>
        <p>Adding an FDU Faculty / Staff E-mail Account to a Mobile Device using the Native E-mail Client</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Step 3: Log on to WebCampus (Blackboard LMS)</h2>
    <div class="content-body">
        <p>Once you have obtained an FDU NetID, you should be able to log on to <a href="{{ webcampus_url }}">{{ webcampus_url }}</a> (Blackboard). Use your FDU NetID login credentials to log on to WebCampus.</p>
        <p>Point your Web browser to <a href="{{ webcampus_login_url }}">{{ webcampus_login_url }}</a> or point your browser to <a href="{{ fdu_url }}">{{ fdu_url }}</a> and locate the "WebCampus" link from the "Web Shortcuts" menu.</p>

        <div class="image-placeholder">
            <!-- Image Placeholder for WebCampus Login -->
            <p>Image of WebCampus Login Screen</p>
        </div>

        <p>For Help and Support with WebCampus / Blackboard</p>
        <p>Students who experience difficulty logging on to WebCampus or technical problems in general should contact the help desk at {{ webcampus_support_phone }} or <a href="mailto:{{ webcampus_support_email }}">{{ webcampus_support_email }}</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Step 4: Access "WebAdvisor"</h2>
    <div class="content-body">
        <p>By using WebAdvisor, you can access your student records to view and print grade reports, transcripts, financial aid documents, and tuition statements.</p>
        <p>Once you have obtained your NetID account, you should be able to log on to WebAdvisor. Use your FDU NetID login credentials to log on to WebAdvisor.</p>
        <p>Point your Web browser to <a href="{{ webadvisor_url }}">{{ webadvisor_url }}</a> or point your browser to <a href="{{ fdu_url }}">{{ fdu_url }}</a> and locate the "WebAdvisor" link from the Web Shortcuts menu.</p>

        <div class="image-placeholder">
            <!-- Image Placeholder for WebAdvisor Login -->
            <p>Image of WebAdvisor Login Screen</p>
        </div>

        <p>WebAdvisor will be available between the hours of {{ webadvisor_start_time }} and {{ webadvisor_end_time }}. During priority registration periods, the system will be available between the hours of {{ webadvisor_priority_start }} and {{ webadvisor_priority_end }}.</p>

        <p>For help and support with WebAdvisor, please email {{ webadvisor_support_email }} or call them at {{ webadvisor_support_phone }}. If you have any technical difficulties using WebAdvisor, please send an email to {{ webadvisor_admin_email }}.</p>
    </div>
</div>


